Paraguay rocked by mass protests after major bank closure freezes millions’ funds

Massive protests have erupted in Paraguay’s capital, Asunción, following the closure of the country’s largest private bank amid a liquidity crisis. Demonstrators are demanding President Santiago Peña’s resignation, with clashes reported between protesters and police. Millions of people have reportedly had their funds frozen, including pension savings.

